# ConsoleLog at top of every managed workflow

Every active managed workflow JSON under `server/workflows/` (not `_done/` / `_inbox/`) must begin with a `ConsoleLog` node.

## Template standard

- Node id: `0` (stable integer id so it stays the first key among Comfy’s numeric node ids; do not invent per-file ids)
- It must be the **first key** in the workflow JSON object
- `class_type`: `ConsoleLog` (from repo `custom_nodes/console_log`)
- Default `inputs.text` is the bordered placeholder from `server/workflows/_console-log.js` (`DEFAULT_CONSOLE_LOG_TEXT`)

```json
{
  "0": {
    "inputs": {
      "text": "=========\nparascene managed run\n(no run details provided)\n========="
    },
    "class_type": "ConsoleLog",
    "_meta": { "title": "Console Log" }
  },
  "...": "rest of graph"
}
```

Use id `0` (not a string name): JSON object key order puts integer-index keys ahead of other strings, so a named id like `parascene_console_log` would sort after nodes such as `29`.

## Runtime standard

- Builders compose the banner in JS via `composeRunConsoleLog` / `ensureConsoleLog` in `server/workflows/_console-log.js`
- `buildWorkflowByFamily` always runs `ensureConsoleLog` so the text is filled from the managed-run payload (workflow id, model, size, seed, duration, media, prompt/lyrics snippet)
- Keep the node first after ensure; do not leave duplicate `ConsoleLog` nodes

## When adding or graduating a workflow

1. Put ConsoleLog as node id `0` at the **top** of the new `.json` template
2. Do not rely on Comfy’s default logs for run identity — the banner is the intentional console signal
3. See `_inbox/console_log_example.json` for node shape only; production text comes from JS
